  "final_text": "All four steps are done.\n\n1. The data view's time field is `timestamp`.\n2. The dashboard \"S4-15bff99e Flights\" has two panels. \"Flights over time\" is a line chart of flight counts by `timestamp`. \"Flights by carrier\" is a bar chart of flight counts by `Carrier`.\n3. The rule \"S4-15bff99e Cancelled flights\" checks every minute. It fires when more than 10 documents with `Cancelled: true` arrive in a 5-minute window. It was created disabled, so I enabled it.\n4. I applied the title edit to the carrier panel, but it was already named \"Flights by carrier\" when I created it, so nothing changed. Reading the rule back shows it enabled, with status \"ok\".\n\nTIME_FIELD: timestamp\nRULE_ENABLED: yes",
